<title>CANADA: Saskatchewan Agriculture details 1996 crop yields.</title>
<headline>Saskatchewan Agriculture details 1996 crop yields.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saskatchewan Agriculture Thursday detailed yields for its 1996 crop.</p>
<p>About three percent of the 1996 crop remained in the field, primarily in the northeast. Production was expected to be 23 percent higer than the previous year at 28.5 million tonnes compared to 23.2 million tonnes.</p>
<p>	  1996 SASKATCHEWAN CROP YIELD ESTIMATES</p>
<p>		 1996 bu/ac 86/95 avg</p>
<p>Winter Wheat 30.1	 21.4</p>
<p>Spring Wheat 32.2	 27.8</p>
<p>Durum Wheat  31.8	 27.5</p>
<p>Oats	   68.3	 55.0</p>
<p>Barley	 55.2	 46.5</p>
<p>Fall Rye     28.1	 25.5</p>
<p>Spring Rye   26.2	 24.7</p>
<p>Flax	   21.9	 18.9</p>
<p>Canola	 23.1	 21.2</p>
<p>SPECIAL CROPS    lbs/ac</p>
<p>Mustard     1,000	 885</p>
<p>Sunflowers  1,102	 926</p>
<p>Lentils     1,266     1,089</p>
<p>Peas	  1,764     1,567</p>
<p>Canary Seed 1,148	 993</p>
<p>--Gilbert Le Gras 204-947-3548</p>
